35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found that two people write all notes by hand, and we lose an hour daily copying records. It feels very heavy for them.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The developers are tied up until Q3, and the integrator left no documentation. We cannot promise dates without that groundwork.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The capital line is frozen, but the software allowance has room. Per-head licences climb with every department added, unlike fixed-fee work.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"So, broad tools die, but niche ones survive. We’re just recycling the same failure. @Midori, does your data match this pattern?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Yes, May. The daily hour lost to copying confirms the friction. We need to address the real, quiet losses, not just the big promises.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@May, I agree. The quiet losses are real. @George, does the frozen budget mean we can’t hire help for those two people?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@George, if the capital line is frozen, we cannot hire external help. We are stuck with the current, unavailable team.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, not entirely. The software allowance has room. We can fund a fixed-fee solution without touching the frozen capital line.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, that’s a lifeline. But if the niche tools survive, why do we keep betting on broad ones? We’re ignoring the data.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, exactly. We keep chasing the impressive pitch while ignoring the daily grind. Let’s focus on solving that specific, quiet friction instead.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@George, if we use the software allowance, will that actually free up those two people? I worry they will just get more work.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, a fixed-fee tool might reduce the copying burden, but it doesn’t solve the access or availability issues. We still lack the groundwork.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Minato, it reduces the manual load, but the real risk is the renewal notice. I need to see if the fixed fee stays flat next year.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
